bitpeer
------------------------------------------
Bitpeer is an experimental Bitcoin relay server. Its event-driven architecture
makes it extremely fast, and it was designed to be very lightweight.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libevent2.1_7-2.1.13-1
  libssl3-3.5.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libevent-devel-2.1.13-1
  libssl-devel-3.5.9-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/TvdW/bitpeer

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/TvdW/bitpeer.git

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack bitpeer-0.2.3+git20130505-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./bitpeer-0.2.3+git20130505-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/bitpeer-0.2.3+git20130505-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/bitpeer-0.2.3+git20130505-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(bitpeer)
  /usr/bin/bitpeer.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/bitpeer.README
  /usr/share/doc/bitpeer/LICENSE.txt
  /usr/share/doc/bitpeer/README.md

